course: dictionary
lesson: 4910
title: Words from faith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one religion or one place of worship. You may not know them, but the sentences around them often give clues. «People pray side by side in rows, led by an imam» tells you that the imam leads the prayers, so an imam must be the person who leads them.
explain: Ask what job the word does in the sentence. Here, the imam stands at the front and leads. Then test your meaning: swap it in and see if the sentence still makes sense. «People pray side by side in rows, led by the person who leads the prayers» works, so your meaning is right.
explain: The sentence also tells you about the place. A mosque is a Muslim place of prayer, and people take off their shoes before they pray. Standing shoulder to shoulder shows that everyone is equal before God.
fact: An imam is the person who leads prayers in a mosque.
fact: An imam often teaches and gives advice to Muslims.
fact: «Imam» is also a title for an important religious leader in Shia Islam, from the Prophet Muhammad's family.
fact: «The imam of the mosque» and «the imam led the prayers» are useful phrases to remember.
fact: A mosque is the Muslim place of prayer, and people face Mecca, the holy city of Islam, when they pray.
exercise: «The imam led the prayers at the mosque.» Who led the prayers? | The shopkeeper | *The imam | The teacher
exercise: An imam often gives advice to Muslims. What does advice mean? | *Helpful suggestions about what to do | A loud shout | A kind of food | A sharp knife
exercise: «Standing shoulder to shoulder shows that everyone is equal.» What does equal mean? | Hungry | Late | *The same, with no one above the others | Very tall
test: In a mosque, people pray together. What is a mosque? | *A Muslim place of prayer | A school for cooking | A shop where people buy bread | A hill with a path up it
test: Which sentence uses the word imam correctly? | I put my imam in the shopping bag | I bought some bread from the imam | *The imam of the mosque led the prayers | The imam was a big red bus
exam: «People face Mecca when they pray.» What is Mecca? | A type of bread | *The holy city of Islam | A river in England | A tall mountain
